Up until this point in my thesis I have mostly used visual studio code as my IDE. I cloned the GitHub from @Vitalis2019#footnote[https://github.com/tudelft3d/cityjson-versioning-prototype/tree/main] to test and modify the code used for the existing VCS. 

Data sources I used to test the VCS:
- Standard geometric shapes from the official CityJSON website #footnote[https://www.cityjson.org/datasets/]
- Tiles from 3DBAG #footnote[https://3dbag.nl/en/download].
- FlatCityBuf#footnote[https://flatcitybuf-prototype.hideba.me/] to download a custom 3D city model.
- Ninja#footnote[https://ninja.cityjson.org/] to visualise CityJSON files


